WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:11.560
Tickets: requests that need the team's reply, ordered by priority and wait time: a complaint, a special request, or a question the assistant couldn't answer.

2
00:00:12.106 --> 00:00:18.530
Tickets marked "Team's turn" are at the top; the "Priority" column and the waiting time are beside each.

3
00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:22.930
"💬 Reply" opens that customer's conversation so you can answer.

4
00:00:23.484 --> 00:00:30.710
When it's done, click "✓ Resolved"; if the customer writes again, the ticket reopens on its own.

5
00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:35.280
Change a ticket's priority so the most important come first.

6
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:43.610
An unresolved ticket means a customer is waiting; if you have no answer yet, at least send a short message that you're on it.
